<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "inLanguage": "en", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "Does a web app work without internet?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "A classic web app requires an internet connection. Web apps developed as PWAs, however, can work offline to a limited extent by caching some data and syncing it when the connection returns. If full, long-term offline operation is required, a desktop app is the safer option."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Is a desktop app or a web app more secure?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Neither is inherently more secure. Web apps are exposed to the internet, so they need strong authentication and regular updates; with desktop apps, backing up local data, device loss and un-updated installations pose risks. Security depends on architecture and maintenance."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Can I convert my desktop program into a web app?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes, but this usually means redevelopment. Business rules and data structures can be preserved, while the interface and infrastructure are redesigned for the web. During the transition, it is important to run both systems in parallel for a while and migrate data carefully."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Is developing a web app cheaper than a desktop app?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "If you are targeting multiple platforms and many users, the total cost is usually lower on the web, because a single codebase runs on all devices and no update distribution is needed. For a hardware-intensive job on a single operating system, a desktop app may be more economical."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Can a web app run on our own server?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. A web app can be hosted on a cloud server or run on your company’s own server, accessible only from the internal network. In cases where data must not leave the organisation, this model keeps the data in-house while preserving the web’s ease of installation and updates."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Does an app built with Electron count as a desktop app?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Electron apps are real desktop apps that are installed on the computer and can access the operating system; their interfaces are written with web technologies. This makes sharing code with a web app easier, but size and memory usage are higher than native apps."}}]}</script>
